ds4: unknown option: ./ds4
Usage: ds4 [(-p PROMPT | --prompt-file FILE)] [options]

Invocation modes:
  ds4
      Start the interactive chat prompt with a session backend: ds4>
  ds4 -p TEXT
      Run one prompt and exit.
  ds4 --prompt-file FILE
      Run one prompt read from FILE and exit. Useful for long prompts.

Model and runtime:
  -m, --model FILE
      GGUF model path. Default: ds4flash.gguf
      A sidecar package directory is also accepted when it contains
      manifest.json and dense/model-dense.gguf.
  --mtp FILE
      Optional MTP support GGUF used for draft-token probes.
  --mtp-draft N
      Maximum autoregressive MTP draft tokens per speculative step. Default: 1
  --mtp-margin F
      Minimum recursive-draft confidence for the fast N=2 verifier. Default: 3
  --draft dspark
      Use a DSpark draft package for speculative decoding. Greedy only.
  --draft-path PATH
      DS4 DSpark draft package directory, e.g. /Users/anemll/Models/DSv4-Flash-DSpark-draft.
  --draft-verify N
      Fixed DSpark verification budget, 1..5. Default: 5
  --draft-verify-dynamic
      Adapt active DSpark verify budget from 2 up to --draft-verify based on recent accepted tokens.
  --draft-mode strict|batch|unified
      DSpark verifier contract. strict keeps no-draft greedy compatibility; batch/unified are experimental.
  --draft-scheduler static|confidence|confidence-softmax
      DSpark verification scheduler. Default: static
  --draft-conf-threshold F
      DSpark confidence threshold for the confidence scheduler. Default: 0
  --dspark-attn-force-mma
      Diagnostic: force DSpark verifier MMA attention path.
  --moe-sidecar PATH
      Flash-MoE sidecar directory containing manifest.json and expert records.
  --moe-mode NAME
      Routed expert weight source: off or slot-bank. Default: off
  --moe-slot-bank N
      Streaming slots per layer; main RAM/cache knob. Default: 32
      Higher caches more experts; lower uses less RAM.
  --resident
      Flash-MoE sidecar resident mode: load every expert into a mixed
      slot bank, request Metal residency, touch pages, and preload all
      routed layers. Implies --moe-mode slot-bank and defaults slots
      per layer to the model expert count.
  --ssd-cache BYTES|auto
      Size the Flash-MoE slot bank from a cache budget such as 25GB.
      auto uses available memory minus dense weights and context buffers,
      then assigns DS4_SSD_CACHE_AUTO_PCT% (default 20) of the remainder
      to the slot bank, leaving headroom for the OS file cache that
      serves decode-miss reads of the sidecar.
  --moe-expert-topk N
      Experimental: route/stream only N experts per token instead of
      the model default. Applies to both prefill and decode.
  -c, --ctx N
      Context size allocated for the session. Default: 32768
  --metal
      Use the Metal graph backend. This is the normal fast path on macOS.
  --cuda
      Use the CUDA graph backend. This is the normal fast path on CUDA builds.
  --cpu
      Use the CPU reference/debug backend. Not recommended for normal inference.
  --backend NAME
      Select backend explicitly: metal, cuda, or cpu.
  -t, --threads N
      CPU helper threads for host-side or reference work.
  --quality
      Prefer exact kernels where faster approximate paths exist; implies --no-int8.
  --no-int8
      Disable int8 accelerator paths; use NAX-half/GPU fallbacks for quality-preserving runs.
  --dir-steering-file FILE
      Load one f32 direction vector per layer for directional steering.
  --dir-steering-ffn F
      Apply steering after FFN outputs: y -= F*v*dot(v,y). Default with file: 1
  --dir-steering-attn F
      Apply steering after attention outputs. Default: 0
  --warm-weights
      Touch mapped tensor pages before generation. Slower startup, fewer first-use stalls.

Prompt and generation:
  -p, --prompt TEXT
      Prompt to generate from.
  --prompt-file FILE
      Read the prompt text from FILE.
  -sys, --system TEXT
      System prompt. Empty string disables the default. Default: You are a helpful assistant
  -n, --tokens N
      Maximum tokens to generate. Default: 50000
  --temp F
      Sampling temperature. 0 is greedy/deterministic. Default: 1
  --top-p F
      Nucleus sampling probability. Default: 1
  --min-p F
      Keep tokens scoring at least F times the top token. Default: 0.05
  --seed N
      Sampling seed for reproducible non-greedy runs. Default: time-based
  --think
      Use normal thinking mode. This is the default.
  --think-max
      Use Think Max when --ctx is at least 393216 tokens; otherwise normal thinking.
  --nothink
      Start assistant turns with </think> for direct non-thinking replies.

Interactive commands:
  /help
      Show interactive commands.
  /think, /think-max, /nothink
      Select normal thinking, context-gated Think Max, or non-thinking mode.
  /ctx N
      Recreate the interactive session with a new context size.
  /read FILE
      Read a prompt from FILE and run it as the next user message.
  /quit, /exit
      Leave the interactive prompt.
  Ctrl+C
      Stop the current generation and return to ds4> without exiting.

Diagnostics:
  --inspect
      Load the model and print a summary only.
  --dump-tokens
      Print the rendered prompt tokens, then exit without inference.
  --dump-logprobs FILE
      Write greedy continuation top-logprobs as JSON without printing text.
  --logprobs-top-k N
      Number of local alternatives stored by --dump-logprobs. Default: 20
  --imatrix-dataset FILE
      Rendered DS4 prompt dataset produced by misc/imatrix_dataset.
  --imatrix-out FILE
      Collect a routed-MoE activation imatrix and write llama-compatible .dat.
  --imatrix-max-prompts N
      Stop imatrix collection after N prompts. Default: no prompt limit
  --imatrix-max-tokens N
      Stop imatrix collection after N prompt tokens. Default: no token limit
  --head-test
      Run the output HC/logits head after the native slice.
  --first-token-test
      Run an exact CPU whole-model pass for the first prompt token.
  --metal-graph-test
      Compare first GPU-resident graph stages with CPU.
  --metal-graph-full-test
      Run the GPU-resident self-token graph across all layers.
  --metal-graph-prompt-test
      Compare CPU and GPU graph logits for the full prompt.

Normal CLI commands:
  ./ds4
  ./ds4 -p "Scrivi una storia su una papera scansafatiche"
  ./ds4 --think-max --prompt-file prompt.txt --ctx 393216

Notes:
  The CLI keeps KV cache state across interactive turns on session backends.
  CPU mode supports interactive chat too, but it is a slow reference/debug path.
  Long added input is processed with batched prefill; short continuations use decode.
  Startup prints the extra context-buffer memory for the selected context size.

  -h, --help
      Show this help.
